# Phase 7: Notes CRUD & Knowledge Base Foundation

## Objective

Replace mock note data with a real database-backed Notes Management System.

This phase establishes the foundation for the upcoming Information Retrieval (IR) module by allowing students to create, manage, and store study notes permanently.

---

## Features Implemented

### Notes Management

* Create Notes
* View Notes
* Edit Notes
* Delete Notes

### Database Integration

* SQLite Notes Table
* User-specific note ownership
* Persistent storage
* Timestamp tracking

### Authentication Integration

* Only authenticated users can access notes
* Users can only manage their own notes

---

## Database Schema

Table: notes

Fields:

* id
* user_id
* title
* content
* created_at
* updated_at

---

## API Endpoints

POST /notes
GET /notes
GET /notes/{id}
PUT /notes/{id}
DELETE /notes/{id}

---

## Frontend Features

### Notes Dashboard

* Notes List
* Create Note Form
* Edit Note Form
* Delete Confirmation

---

## Mock Data Removal

Previous Source:

INITIAL_NOTES (mockData.js)

New Source:

SQLite Database via FastAPI APIs

---

## Why This Phase Matters

The Information Retrieval module requires real user-generated study material.

Phase 7 provides the document repository that will later be used for:

* Tokenization
* Stopword Removal
* Lemmatization
* TF-IDF Vectorization
* Inverted Index Creation
* Cosine Similarity Search
* Document Ranking

This phase serves as the bridge between the application infrastructure and the upcoming IR engine.
